/-!
# Closure under extensions of the finite type locally constant sheaves of modules

Let `(C, J)` be a site and `Λ` a left Noetherian ring, not assumed commutative. Stacks
Tag 093U (3) asserts that the finite type locally constant sheaves of `Λ`-modules form a weak
Serre subcategory of `Mod(C, Λ)`. Four of the five conditions of Tag 0754 are proved in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocallyConstantSerreClass`; this file proves the
fifth, closure under extensions, and concludes the tag.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.trivSection`: the section of `F` over an object of `C/Z` attached to an
  element of `E` by a trivialization `E̲ ≅ F|_{C/Z}`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extSubmodule`: given a map `a : M →ₗ T` and a finite family `t` in `T`,
  the submodule of `T` they generate. Applied with `T` the sections of the middle term of the
  short exact sequence over an object, `a` cut out by a trivialization of the first term and `t`
  a family of lifts of generators of the third term, this is the module on which the middle term
  becomes constant.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extInl` and `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extProj`: the two maps exhibiting that
  module as an extension of `N` by `M`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isIso_of_shortExact_of_comm`: the short five lemma.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_section_of_apply_eq_zero`: sections of a short exact sequence of
  sheaves are left exact over each object.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isConstantFGOver_X₂_of_lifts`: the core construction — given lifts of
  generators and witnesses for the relations, the middle term is constant.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.trivSieve_X₂_mem`: over an object trivializing both ends, the middle term
  is trivialized on a covering family.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isClosedUnderExtensions_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf` and
  `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isWeakSerreClass_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf`, **Tag 093U (3)**.

## Implementation notes

**The ring is not assumed commutative.** Tag 093U reads `Λ` as a commutative ring, but nothing
in the statement or in this proof needs that: `ModuleCat Λ` and its sheaves are defined for any
ring, `ModuleCat.isFG` is a property of left modules, and `IsNoetherianRing Λ` is the left
Noetherian condition, which is what makes the relations module of a finitely generated module
finitely generated. The generalisation matters because the module data of Tag 03TX, hence of
Tag 03TY, is an arbitrary finite — possibly noncommutative — ring. The one place where the
commutative route had to be replaced is the engine of Tag 093S: see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafLocalHom`.

**No free module of finite rank is used, and this is forced.** Stacks presents `N` as a quotient
of `Λ^{⊕m}` and lifts the resulting map to the middle term. That argument is unavailable here:
the module universe is `max u v w` while `Λ : Type r` is at an unrelated universe, so there need
be *no* finite free `Λ`-module at all in `ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ` — a finite free module has `Λ`
itself as a summand. Instead the module on which the middle term becomes constant is produced
*inside* the sections of the middle term, as the submodule generated by the image of `M` and the
chosen lifts (`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extSubmodule`); its carrier is a subtype of a module already
in the right universe. The relations module `ker (Λ^{⊕m} → N)` is still used, but only as a plain
module, never as an object of the sheaf category, so its universe is irrelevant. Consequently no
smallness hypothesis on `Λ` is added to Tag 093U.

**The degenerate case.** The comparison between the submodule of sections and the middle term
needs the canonical map `N ⟶ Γ(Z, N̲)` to be injective, and that holds exactly when `Z` is not
covered by the empty sieve: for the constant presheaf the equalizer sieve of two distinct
elements is `⊥`, so local injectivity of sheafification forces `⊥ ∈ J Z` otherwise
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.injective_sliceUnit`). When `⊥ ∈ J Z` the localized topology is the
trivial one, every sheaf on `C/Z` is a zero object, and the conclusion is immediate
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isConstantFGOver_of_bot_mem`). The same phenomenon is the hypothesis
`∃ U, ⊥ ∉ J U` of Tag 093N; here it is not a hypothesis because the degenerate case is a
*separate*, and trivial, case rather than an obstruction.

**One spelling per statement.** The result type of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.trivSection` is ascribed
as sections of `F` over an object of `C`, where the body produces sections of the restriction of
`F` to `C/Z`. The two are definitionally equal and not syntactically equal, so `rw` and `simp`
refuse a goal that mixes them; `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.trivSection_apply` is the `rfl`-lemma that
crosses the boundary, and the naturality squares are introduced through `have`s with ascribed
types rather than through `rw`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0754](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0754)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093N)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite ZeroObject

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

universe v u w r

/-! ### Sections of a short exact sequence of sheaves -/

section Sections

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]

/-- Evaluation at an object of the site is a left exact functor on sheaves: it is the composition
of the inclusion of sheaves into presheaves, a right adjoint, with evaluation on presheaves. -/
@[sga "4 I 5.8.3" "Clause 1, special case", sga "4 V 2.4.2" "special case"]
instance preservesFiniteLimits_sheafSections (Z : C) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits ((sheafSections J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj (op Z)) :=
  preservesFiniteLimits_of_natIso
    (sheafSectionsNatIsoEvaluation J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) (X := Z)).symm

variable {J Λ}

/-- **Sections of a short exact sequence are left exact.** A section of the middle term killed by
the second map is the image of a section of the first term, over the same object. -/
theorem exists_section_of_apply_eq_zero
    {S : ShortComplex (Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ))} (hS : S.ShortExact) (Z : C)
    (z : S.X₂.obj.obj (op Z)) (hz : (S.g.hom.app (op Z)).hom z = 0) :
    ∃ y : S.X₁.obj.obj (op Z), (S.f.hom.app (op Z)).hom y = z := by
  have hex : (S.map ((sheafSections J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj (op Z))).Exact :=
    ShortComplex.exact_of_f_is_kernel _
      (KernelFork.mapIsLimit _ hS.fIsKernel
        ((sheafSections J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj (op Z)))
  rw [ShortComplex.moduleCat_exact_iff] at hex
  exact hex z hz

end Sections

/-! ### The degenerate case of an object covered by the empty sieve -/

section Degenerate

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]

/-- If an object is covered by the empty sieve, the localized topology at it is the trivial
topology, so every sheaf on the slice site is a zero object. -/
theorem isZero_overPullback_of_bot_mem {Z : C} (hZ : (⊥ : Sieve Z) ∈ J Z)
    (F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)) :
    IsZero ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj F) := by
  have htop : J.over Z = ⊤ := by
    refine le_antisymm le_top (fun V => ?_)
    intro T _
    rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff]
    refine J.superset_covering bot_le ?_
    simpa using J.pullback_stable V.hom hZ
  exact IsZero.of_iso (isZero_zero _)
    ((Sheaf.isTerminalOfEqTop htop _).uniqueUpToIso (HasZeroObject.zeroIsTerminal))

/-- If an object is covered by the empty sieve, every sheaf trivializes over it: both the
restriction and the constant sheaf on the zero module are zero objects. -/
theorem isConstantFGOver_of_bot_mem {Z : C} (hZ : (⊥ : Sieve Z) ∈ J Z)
    (F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)) : IsConstantFGOver J Λ Z F :=
  ⟨0, isFG_of_isZero Λ (isZero_zero _),
    ⟨IsZero.iso ((constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).map_isZero
        (isZero_zero _)) (isZero_overPullback_of_bot_mem J Λ hZ F)⟩⟩

end Degenerate

/-! ### Morphisms out of a constant sheaf on a slice site -/

section ConstantHom

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]

/-- The canonical map from a module to the sections of the constant sheaf it generates on the
slice site `C/Z`, read off at the terminal object `𝟙 Z`. -/
noncomputable abbrev sliceUnit (Z : C) (E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) :
    E ⟶ ((constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E).obj.obj
      (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))) :=
  constantUnitApp (J.over Z) E (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))

/-- **Morphisms out of a constant sheaf are sections.** Composing with the canonical map out of
the module is a bijection from morphisms `E̲ ⟶ G` of sheaves on `C/Z` to module maps from `E` to
the sections of `G` over the terminal object. This is the constant
sheaf adjunction read through `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheafAdj_homEquiv_apply`. -/
theorem bijective_sliceUnit_comp (Z : C) (E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)
    (G : Sheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)) :
    Function.Bijective (fun φ : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ⟶ G =>
      sliceUnit J Λ Z E ≫ φ.hom.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))) := by
  have h : (fun φ : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ⟶ G =>
      sliceUnit J Λ Z E ≫ φ.hom.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))) =
      (constantSheafAdj (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := Z))).homEquiv
        E G := by
    funext φ
    exact (constantSheafAdj_homEquiv_apply (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)
      Over.mkIdTerminal E G φ).symm
  rw [h]
  exact Equiv.bijective _

end ConstantHom

/-! ### Sections attached to a trivialization -/

section TrivSection

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]

/-- The comparison isomorphism `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.mapPullbackConstantSheafApp` carries the
canonical map out of the constant presheaf on `C/Z` to the canonical map out of the constant
presheaf on `C/Y`. This is the analogue for the relocalization functor `Over.map w` of
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.toSheafify_overPullbackConstantSheafIso`, and like it, it is the
compatibility of sheafification with restriction along a functor which is both continuous and
cocontinuous, read off at one object. -/
theorem constantUnit_mapPullbackConstantSheafApp (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (A : Type*) [Category A] {Y Z : C} (w : Z ⟶ Y)
    [HasWeakSheafify (J.over Z) A] [HasWeakSheafify (J.over Y) A]
    [∀ (G : (Over Z)ᵒᵖ ⥤ A), (Over.map w).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension G]
    (E : A) (V : (Over Z)ᵒᵖ) :
    (toSheafify (J.over Z) ((Functor.const (Over Z)ᵒᵖ).obj E)).app V ≫
        (mapPullbackConstantSheafApp J A w E).hom.hom.app V =
      (toSheafify (J.over Y) ((Functor.const (Over Y)ᵒᵖ).obj E)).app
        ((Over.map w).op.obj V) :=
  congrArg (fun α => NatTrans.app α V)
    ((Over.map w).toSheafify_pullbackSheafificationCompatibility A (J.over Z) (J.over Y)
      ((Functor.const (Over Y)ᵒᵖ).obj E))

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Λ : Type r} [Ring Λ]
variable {F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)}

/-- **The sections cut out by a trivialization.** A trivialization `α` of `F` over `Z` by the
constant sheaf on `E` sends an element of `E` to a section of `F` over any object `V` of `C/Z`:
take the canonical image of the element in the sections of `E̲` and apply `α`. -/
noncomputable def trivSection {Z : C} {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    (α : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj F) (V : Over Z) :
    E ⟶ F.obj.obj (op V.left) :=
  constantUnitApp (J.over Z) E (op V) ≫ α.hom.hom.app (op V)

/-- The value of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.trivSection` on an element. Stated separately because the
result type of that definition is ascribed as sections of `F` over an object of `C`, where the
body produces sections of the restriction of `F` to `C/Z`; the two are definitionally equal and
not syntactically equal, so `rw` and `simp` refuse a goal that mixes them. -/
theorem trivSection_apply {Z : C} {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    {α : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj F} (V : Over Z) (e : E) :
    (trivSection α V).hom e =
      (α.hom.hom.app (op V)).hom ((constantUnitApp (J.over Z) E (op V)).hom e) :=
  rfl

/-- The sections cut out by a trivialization are compatible with restriction in `C/Z`. -/
theorem trivSection_restrict {Z : C} {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    {α : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj F} {V V' : Over Z} (g : V' ⟶ V) (e : E) :
    (F.obj.map g.left.op).hom ((trivSection α V).hom e) = (trivSection α V').hom e := by
  have h := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (α.hom.hom.naturality g.op)
    ((constantUnitApp (J.over Z) E (op V)).hom e)
  simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] at h
  rw [map_constantUnitApp] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- The sections cut out by a trivialization of `F` over `Y`, read at an object lying over `Y`. -/
noncomputable abbrev trivSectionAt {Y : C} {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    (α : (constantSheaf (J.over Y) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Y).obj F) {Z : C} (w : Z ⟶ Y) :
    E ⟶ F.obj.obj (op Z) :=
  trivSection α (Over.mk w)

/-- The sections cut out by a trivialization over `Y` are compatible with restriction along a
morphism `w' : Z' ⟶ Z` of objects lying over `Y`. -/
theorem trivSectionAt_comp {Y : C} {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    {α : (constantSheaf (J.over Y) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Y).obj F} {Z Z' : C} (w : Z ⟶ Y) (w' : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (e : E) :
    (F.obj.map w'.op).hom ((trivSectionAt α w).hom e) = (trivSectionAt α (w' ≫ w)).hom e :=
  trivSection_restrict (Over.homMk w' : Over.mk (w' ≫ w) ⟶ Over.mk w) e

/-- **Restricting a trivialization does not change the sections it cuts out.** The trivialization
of `F` over `Z` obtained from one over `Y` by `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.restrictTrivIso` sends an
element of `E` to the same section of `F` over `Z`. -/
theorem trivSection_restrictTrivIso {Y Z : C} (w : Z ⟶ Y) {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ}
    (α : (constantSheaf (J.over Y) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Y).obj F) (e : E) :
    (trivSection (restrictTrivIso J Λ w E α) (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom e =
      (trivSectionAt α w).hom e := by
  have hu := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (constantUnit_mapPullbackConstantSheafApp J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) w E
      (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))) e
  have hid : (trivSection α (Over.mk (𝟙 Z ≫ w))).hom e = (trivSectionAt α w).hom e := by
    have h := trivSectionAt_comp (α := α) w (𝟙 Z) e
    simp only [op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, ModuleCat.hom_id, LinearMap.id_coe,
      id_eq] at h
    exact h.symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ hid
  exact congrArg
    (fun x => ((α.hom).hom.app (op ((Over.map w).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))))).hom x) hu

end TrivSection

/-! ### Injectivity of the canonical map on a non-degenerate object -/

section Injective

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]

/-- **The canonical map is injective off the degenerate case**, on the slice site. This is
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.injective_constantUnitApp` for the localized topology at `Z` and the
terminal object `𝟙 Z` of `C/Z`, whose covering sieves are read in `C` by
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff`. -/
theorem injective_sliceUnit {Z : C} (hbot : (⊥ : Sieve Z) ∉ J Z)
    (E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) : Function.Injective (sliceUnit J Λ Z E).hom := by
  refine injective_constantUnitApp (J.over Z) E (fun hb => hbot ?_)
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hb
  simpa using hb

end Injective

/-! ### The module generated by the image of `M` and a family of lifts -/

section ModuleAlgebra

variable {Λ : Type r} [Ring Λ]
variable {M N T T' : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module Λ M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module Λ N]
  [AddCommGroup T] [Module Λ T] [AddCommGroup T'] [Module Λ T']
variable (a : M →ₗ[Λ] T) {m : ℕ} (t : Fin m → T)

/-- The map assembling a map out of `M` and a family of `m` elements of `T` into a map out of
`M ⊕ Λ^m`. -/
def extAssemble : (M × (Fin m → Λ)) →ₗ[Λ] T :=
  a ∘ₗ LinearMap.fst Λ M (Fin m → Λ) +
    Fintype.linearCombination Λ t ∘ₗ LinearMap.snd Λ M (Fin m → Λ)

/-- The value of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extAssemble` on a pair `(c, l)` is
`a c + ∑ j, l j • t j`. -/
theorem extAssemble_apply (z : M × (Fin m → Λ)) :
    extAssemble a t z = a z.1 + ∑ j, z.2 j • t j := rfl

/-- **The module of an extension datum.** The submodule of `T` generated by the image of `M` and
the family `t`. When `T` is the module of sections of the middle term of a short exact sequence
over an object, `a` is the map cut out by a trivialization of the first term and `t` is a family
of lifts of generators of the third term, this is the module on which the middle term becomes
constant. -/
def extSubmodule : Submodule Λ T := LinearMap.range (extAssemble a t)

/-- An element of `T` lies in the module of an extension datum if and only if it is of the form
`a c + ∑ j, l j • t j`. -/
theorem mem_extSubmodule {z : T} :
    z ∈ extSubmodule a t ↔ ∃ (c : M) (l : Fin m → Λ), a c + ∑ j, l j • t j = z :=
  ⟨fun ⟨⟨c, l⟩, h⟩ => ⟨c, l, h⟩, fun ⟨c, l, h⟩ => ⟨(c, l), h⟩⟩

/-- The image of `M` lies in the module of an extension datum. -/
theorem a_mem_extSubmodule (c : M) : a c ∈ extSubmodule a t :=
  ⟨(c, 0), by simp [extAssemble_apply]⟩

/-- The map from `M` to the module of an extension datum. -/
def extInl : M →ₗ[Λ] (extSubmodule a t) :=
  LinearMap.codRestrict _ a (a_mem_extSubmodule a t)

/-- The map `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extInl`, followed by the inclusion into `T`, is `a`. -/
@[simp] theorem extInl_coe (c : M) : ((extInl a t c : extSubmodule a t) : T) = a c := rfl

/-- The module of an extension datum is finitely generated when `M` is. -/
theorem finite_extSubmodule [Module.Finite Λ M] : Module.Finite Λ (extSubmodule a t) :=
  Module.Finite.of_surjective (extAssemble a t).rangeRestrict
    (LinearMap.surjective_rangeRestrict _)

variable (g : T →ₗ[Λ] T') (b : N →ₗ[Λ] T') (y : Fin m → N)
variable (hag : ∀ c : M, g (a c) = 0) (ht : ∀ j, g (t j) = b (y j))

/-- If `g` kills the image of `M` and sends each `t j` to `b (y j)`, then `g` sends
`a c + ∑ j, l j • t j` to `b (∑ j, l j • y j)`. -/
private theorem apply_add_sum_smul_eq (hag : ∀ c : M, g (a c) = 0)
    (ht : ∀ j, g (t j) = b (y j)) (c : M) (l : Fin m → Λ) :
    g (a c + ∑ j, l j • t j) = b (∑ j, l j • y j) := by
  rw [map_add, hag, zero_add, map_sum, map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [map_smul, map_smul, ht]

include hag ht in
/-- If `g` kills the image of `M` and sends each `t j` to `b (y j)`, then `g` maps the module of
an extension datum into the range of `b`. -/
theorem map_mem_range_of_mem_extSubmodule (z : extSubmodule a t) :
    g (z : T) ∈ LinearMap.range b := by
  obtain ⟨c, l, h⟩ := (mem_extSubmodule a t).1 z.2
  exact ⟨∑ j, l j • y j, h ▸ (apply_add_sum_smul_eq a t g b y hag ht c l).symm⟩

variable (hb : Function.Injective b)

/-- The map from the module of an extension datum to `N`: the second map of the short exact
sequence it sits in. It is characterised by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.b_extProj`. -/
noncomputable def extProj : (extSubmodule a t) →ₗ[Λ] N :=
  (LinearEquiv.ofInjective b hb).symm ∘ₗ
    LinearMap.codRestrict (LinearMap.range b) (g ∘ₗ (extSubmodule a t).subtype)
      (map_mem_range_of_mem_extSubmodule a t g b y hag ht)

include hag ht in
/-- The composite of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extProj` with `b` is the restriction of `g` to the
module of an extension datum. -/
theorem b_extProj (z : extSubmodule a t) :
    b (extProj a t g b y hag ht hb z) = g (z : T) :=
  congrArg Subtype.val ((LinearEquiv.ofInjective b hb).apply_symm_apply
    (LinearMap.codRestrict (LinearMap.range b) (g ∘ₗ (extSubmodule a t).subtype)
      (map_mem_range_of_mem_extSubmodule a t g b y hag ht) z))

include hag ht in
/-- The composite of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extInl` and `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extProj` is zero. -/
theorem extProj_extInl (c : M) : extProj a t g b y hag ht hb (extInl a t c) = 0 := by
  refine hb ?_
  rw [b_extProj, extInl_coe, hag, map_zero]

include hag ht in
/-- The second map of the extension datum sequence is surjective when `y` generates `N`. -/
theorem surjective_extProj (hy : Submodule.span Λ (Set.range y) = ⊤) :
    Function.Surjective (extProj a t g b y hag ht hb) := by
  intro n
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ : ∃ l : Fin m → Λ, ∑ j, l j • y j = n := by
    rw [← Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun, hy]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  refine ⟨⟨a 0 + ∑ j, l j • t j, ⟨(0, l), rfl⟩⟩, hb ?_⟩
  rw [b_extProj, ← hl]
  exact apply_add_sum_smul_eq a t g b y hag ht 0 l

include hag ht in
/-- The extension datum sequence is exact in the middle: an element of the module killed by the
map to `N` lies in the image of `M`. This is where the generators of the relation module between
the chosen generators of `N` are used, and it is the only place where the hypothesis that each
relation is realised by an element of `M` enters. -/
theorem exists_extInl_eq_of_extProj_eq_zero {p : ℕ} (κ : Fin p → (Fin m → Λ))
    (hκ : LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) ≤ Submodule.span Λ (Set.range κ))
    (x : Fin p → M) (hx : ∀ i, a (x i) = ∑ j, κ i j • t j)
    (z : extSubmodule a t) (hz : extProj a t g b y hag ht hb z = 0) :
    ∃ c : M, extInl a t c = z := by
  obtain ⟨c, l, hcl⟩ := (mem_extSubmodule a t).1 z.2
  have hl0 : (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) l = 0 := by
    refine hb ?_
    have h1 : b ((Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) l) = g (z : T) := by
      rw [Fintype.linearCombination_apply, ← hcl]
      exact (apply_add_sum_smul_eq a t g b y hag ht c l).symm
    rw [h1, ← b_extProj a t g b y hag ht hb z, hz, map_zero]
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ : ∃ μ : Fin p → Λ, ∑ i, μ i • κ i = l := by
    rw [← Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun]
    exact hκ hl0
  refine ⟨c + ∑ i, μ i • x i, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  rw [extInl_coe, ← hcl, map_add, map_sum]
  congr 1
  rw [← hμ]
  simp only [Finset.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Finset.sum_smul, mul_smul,
    map_smul, hx, Finset.smul_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_comm

end ModuleAlgebra

/-! ### The short five lemma -/

section ShortFive

/-- **The short five lemma.** A morphism of short exact sequences in an abelian category which is
an isomorphism on both ends is an isomorphism in the middle. This is assembled from Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.mono_of_mono_of_mono_of_mono` and
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.epi_of_epi_of_epi_of_epi` together with balancedness. -/
theorem isIso_of_shortExact_of_comm {A : Type*} [Category A] [Abelian A]
    {R₁ R₂ : ShortComplex A} (h₁ : R₁.ShortExact) (h₂ : R₂.ShortExact)
    (τ₁ : R₁.X₁ ⟶ R₂.X₁) (τ₂ : R₁.X₂ ⟶ R₂.X₂) (τ₃ : R₁.X₃ ⟶ R₂.X₃)
    (c₁ : τ₁ ≫ R₂.f = R₁.f ≫ τ₂) (c₂ : τ₂ ≫ R₂.g = R₁.g ≫ τ₃)
    [IsIso τ₁] [IsIso τ₃] : IsIso τ₂ := by
  have hm : Mono τ₂ :=
    ShortComplex.mono_of_mono_of_mono_of_mono (ShortComplex.homMk τ₁ τ₂ τ₃ c₁ c₂)
      h₁.exact h₂.mono_f (inferInstanceAs (Mono τ₁)) (inferInstanceAs (Mono τ₃))
  have he : Epi τ₂ :=
    ShortComplex.epi_of_epi_of_epi_of_epi (ShortComplex.homMk τ₁ τ₂ τ₃ c₁ c₂)
      h₂.exact h₁.epi_g (inferInstanceAs (Epi τ₁)) (inferInstanceAs (Epi τ₃))
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi τ₂

end ShortFive

/-! ### The core construction -/

section Core

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]

/-- The constant sheaf functor on a slice site preserves finite limits: it is the constant
presheaf functor, which preserves all limits because limits of presheaves are computed pointwise,
followed by sheafification, which is left exact. -/
@[sga "4 I 5.8.3" "Clause 1, special case"]
instance preservesFiniteLimits_constantSheaf_over (Z : C) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)) := by
  dsimp only [constantSheaf]
  exact comp_preservesFiniteLimits _ _

variable {J Λ}

/-- An isomorphism of sheaves of modules is injective on sections over any object. -/
theorem injective_app_of_iso {F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)} (e : F ≅ G) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Injective (e.hom.hom.app X).hom := by
  have h1 : IsIso e.hom.hom := inferInstance
  have h : IsIso (e.hom.hom.app X) := inferInstance
  exact (ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective _).1 inferInstance

/-- Evaluating an isomorphism of sheaves of modules and its inverse on sections. -/
theorem iso_app_inv_app {F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)} (e : F ≅ G) (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (z : G.obj.obj X) : (e.hom.hom.app X).hom ((e.inv.hom.app X).hom z) = z := by
  have h : e.inv.hom.app X ≫ e.hom.hom.app X = 𝟙 _ := by
    rw [← NatTrans.comp_app, ← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, e.inv_hom_id]
    rfl
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h z

variable {S : ShortComplex (Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ))}

/-- A trivialization is injective on sections over the terminal object of the slice site. -/
theorem injective_trivSection {Z : C} (hbot : (⊥ : Sieve Z) ∉ J Z)
    {E : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ} {F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)}
    (α : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj F) :
    Function.Injective (trivSection α (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom := by
  intro c c' h
  rw [trivSection_apply, trivSection_apply] at h
  exact injective_sliceUnit J Λ hbot E (injective_app_of_iso α _ h)

/-- **The core construction for closure under extensions.** Suppose a short exact sequence of
sheaves of `Λ`-modules becomes, over `Z`, an extension of the constant sheaf on `N` by the
constant sheaf on `M` with `M` finitely generated; suppose `y` generates `N`, that `κ` generates
the module of relations between the `y`, that each `y j` lifts to a section `t j` of the middle
term over `Z`, and that each relation `κ i` is witnessed by an element `x i` of `M`. Then the
middle term becomes constant over `Z`, on the finitely generated module
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.extSubmodule` generated by the image of `M` and the lifts.

The short exact sequence of modules produced by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_extInl_eq_of_extProj_eq_zero` becomes, under the exact functor
`constantSheaf`, a short exact sequence of sheaves which maps to the given one by the identity on
both ends, so the comparison in the middle is an isomorphism by the short five lemma. -/
theorem isConstantFGOver_X₂_of_lifts (hS : S.ShortExact) {Z : C}
    {M N : ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ} (hM : ModuleCat.isFG Λ M)
    (α : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj M ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj S.X₁)
    (β : (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj N ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj S.X₃)
    {m p : ℕ} (y : Fin m → N) (hy : Submodule.span Λ (Set.range y) = ⊤)
    (κ : Fin p → (Fin m → Λ))
    (hκ : LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) ≤ Submodule.span Λ (Set.range κ))
    (t : Fin m → S.X₂.obj.obj (op Z)) (x : Fin p → M)
    (ht : ∀ j, (S.g.hom.app (op Z)).hom (t j) = (trivSection β (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom (y j))
    (hx : ∀ i, (S.f.hom.app (op Z)).hom ((trivSection α (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom (x i)) =
      ∑ j, κ i j • t j) :
    IsConstantFGOver J Λ Z S.X₂ := by
  classical
  by_cases hbot : (⊥ : Sieve Z) ∈ J Z
  · exact isConstantFGOver_of_bot_mem J Λ hbot S.X₂
  have hMfin : Module.Finite Λ (M : Type (max u v w)) := hM
  have hfinj : Function.Injective (S.f.hom.app (op Z)).hom := by
    have := hS.mono_f
    exact (ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective _).1 inferInstance
  -- the three linear maps of the datum
  set aL : (M : Type (max u v w)) →ₗ[Λ] S.X₂.obj.obj (op Z) :=
    (S.f.hom.app (op Z)).hom ∘ₗ (trivSection α (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom with haL
  set gL : (S.X₂.obj.obj (op Z) : Type (max u v w)) →ₗ[Λ] S.X₃.obj.obj (op Z) :=
    (S.g.hom.app (op Z)).hom with hgL
  set bL : (N : Type (max u v w)) →ₗ[Λ] S.X₃.obj.obj (op Z) :=
    (trivSection β (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))).hom with hbL
  have hag : ∀ c : (M : Type (max u v w)), gL (aL c) = 0 := fun c =>
    (S.map ((sheafSections J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj (op Z))).moduleCat_zero_apply _
  have hbinj : Function.Injective bL := injective_trivSection hbot β
  have hainj : Function.Injective aL := hfinj.comp (injective_trivSection hbot α)
  have ht' : ∀ j, gL (t j) = bL (y j) := ht
  have hx' : ∀ i, aL (x i) = ∑ j, κ i j • t j := hx
  have hPfin : Module.Finite Λ (extSubmodule aL t) := finite_extSubmodule aL t
  -- the short exact sequence of modules
  have hzero : ModuleCat.ofHom (extInl aL t) ≫
      ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj) = 0 :=
    ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext fun c => by
      simpa using extProj_extInl aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj c
  have hmono : Mono (ModuleCat.ofHom (extInl aL t)) :=
    (ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective _).2 fun c c' h => hainj (congrArg Subtype.val h)
  have hepi : Epi (ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj)) :=
    (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).2 (surjective_extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj hy)
  have hSP : (ShortComplex.mk (ModuleCat.ofHom (extInl aL t))
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj)) hzero).ShortExact := by
    refine { exact := ?_ }
    rw [ShortComplex.moduleCat_exact_iff]
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_extInl_eq_of_extProj_eq_zero aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj κ hκ x hx'
      z (by simpa using hz)
    exact ⟨c, by simpa using hc⟩
  -- the comparison morphism out of the constant sheaf on the module just built
  obtain ⟨θ, hθ⟩ := (bijective_sliceUnit_comp J Λ Z (ModuleCat.of Λ (extSubmodule aL t))
    ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).obj S.X₂)).2
    (ModuleCat.ofHom (extSubmodule aL t).subtype)
  have hθ' : ∀ z : extSubmodule aL t,
      (θ.hom.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))).hom
        ((sliceUnit J Λ Z (ModuleCat.of Λ (extSubmodule aL t))).hom z) = z.1 := fun z =>
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hθ z
  -- the two squares
  have hc₁ : α.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.f =
      (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (extInl aL t)) ≫ θ := by
    refine (bijective_sliceUnit_comp J Λ Z M _).1 ?_
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun c => ?_)
    have hR := app_constantUnitApp_map (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.ofHom (extInl aL t))
      (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))) c
    simp only [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, NatTrans.comp_app, ModuleCat.hom_comp,
      LinearMap.comp_apply]
    rw [hR, hθ']
    rfl
  have hc₂ : θ ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.g =
      (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj)) ≫ β.hom := by
    refine (bijective_sliceUnit_comp J Λ Z (ModuleCat.of Λ (extSubmodule aL t)) _).1 ?_
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_)
    have hR := app_constantUnitApp_map (J.over Z)
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj)) (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))) z
    simp only [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, NatTrans.comp_app, ModuleCat.hom_comp,
      LinearMap.comp_apply]
    rw [hR, hθ']
    exact (b_extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj z).symm
  -- the target short exact sequence
  have hzero' : (α.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.f) ≫
      ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.g ≫ β.inv) = 0 := by
    rw [Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.f),
      ← Functor.map_comp, S.zero, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_zero, zero_comp, comp_zero]
  have hSE : (ShortComplex.mk (α.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.f)
      ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.g ≫ β.inv) hzero').ShortExact := by
    refine ShortComplex.shortExact_of_iso ?_
      (hS.map_of_exact (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z))
    exact ShortComplex.isoMk α.symm (Iso.refl _) β.symm (by simp) (by simp)
  -- the comparison of short complexes and the short five lemma
  have hφcomm₂ : θ ≫ ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ) Z).map S.g ≫ β.inv) =
      (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (extProj aL t gL bL y hag ht' hbinj)) ≫ 𝟙 _ := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, hc₂, Category.assoc, β.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]
  have hSPcs := hSP.map_of_exact (constantSheaf (J.over Z) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ))
  have hiso : IsIso θ :=
    isIso_of_shortExact_of_comm hSPcs hSE (𝟙 _) θ (𝟙 _)
      (by rwa [Category.id_comp]) hφcomm₂
  exact ⟨ModuleCat.of Λ (extSubmodule aL t), hPfin, ⟨asIso θ⟩⟩

end Core

/-! ### Closure under extensions -/

section Closure

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
variable {Λ : Type r} [Ring Λ]

variable [IsNoetherianRing Λ] {S : ShortComplex (Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ))}

/-- **Local constancy of the middle term of a short exact sequence.** -/
theorem trivSieve_X₂_mem (hS : S.ShortExact) {Y₀ : C}
    (hF : IsConstantFGOver J Λ Y₀ S.X₁) (hG : IsConstantFGOver J Λ Y₀ S.X₃) :
    trivSieve J Λ S.X₂ Y₀ ∈ J Y₀ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨M, hM, ⟨α⟩⟩ := hF
  obtain ⟨N, hN, ⟨β⟩⟩ := hG
  have hNfin : Module.Finite Λ (N : Type (max u v w)) := hN
  obtain ⟨m, y, hy⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin (R := Λ) (M := (N : Type (max u v w)))
  have hKfin : Module.Finite Λ (LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y)) :=
    Module.Finite.iff_fg.2 (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  obtain ⟨p, κ', hκ'⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin (R := Λ)
    (M := (LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y)))
  have hκ : LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) ≤
      Submodule.span Λ (Set.range fun i => ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ))) := by
    intro l hl
    have h1 : (⟨l, hl⟩ : LinearMap.ker (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y)) ∈
        Submodule.span Λ (Set.range κ') := by
      rw [hκ']
      exact Submodule.mem_top
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun Λ).1 h1
    rw [Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun Λ]
    exact ⟨c, by simpa using congrArg Subtype.val hc⟩
  have hls : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J S.g.hom := by
    have := hS.epi_g
    have h : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective S.g := by
      rw [Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi']
      infer_instance
    exact h
  refine trivSieve_mem_of_cover (finset_inf_covering J Finset.univ
    (fun j : Fin m => Presheaf.imageSieve S.g.hom
      ((trivSection β (Over.mk (𝟙 Y₀))).hom (y j)))
    (fun j _ => Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J S.g.hom _)) ?_
  intro Z₁ ww hww
  have hlift : ∀ j : Fin m, ∃ s : S.X₂.obj.obj (op Z₁),
      (S.g.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom s = (trivSection β (Over.mk ww)).hom (y j) := by
    intro j
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := sieve_apply_of_le (Finset.inf_le (Finset.mem_univ j)) hww
    exact ⟨s, by
      rw [hs]
      exact trivSection_restrict (Over.homMk ww : Over.mk ww ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 Y₀)) (y j)⟩
  choose t ht using hlift
  have hgz : ∀ i : Fin p,
      (S.g.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom (∑ j, ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ) j) • t j) = 0 := by
    intro i
    have h2 : (Fintype.linearCombination Λ y) (κ' i : Fin m → Λ) = 0 := (κ' i).2
    rw [Fintype.linearCombination_apply] at h2
    calc (S.g.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom (∑ j, ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ) j) • t j)
        = ∑ j, ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ) j) • (trivSection β (Over.mk ww)).hom (y j) := by
          rw [map_sum]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [map_smul, ht j]
      _ = (trivSection β (Over.mk ww)).hom (∑ j, ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ) j) • y j) := by
          simp only [map_sum, map_smul]
      _ = 0 := by rw [h2, map_zero]
  have hsec : ∀ i : Fin p, ∃ s : S.X₁.obj.obj (op Z₁),
      (S.f.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom s = ∑ j, ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ) j) • t j := fun i =>
    exists_section_of_apply_eq_zero hS Z₁ _ (hgz i)
  choose uu huu using hsec
  have hcov₂ : (Finset.univ.inf (fun i : Fin p => Presheaf.imageSieve
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over Y₀) ((Functor.const (Over Y₀)ᵒᵖ).obj M))
      ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i)))) ∈ (J.over Y₀) (Over.mk ww) :=
    finset_inf_covering (J.over Y₀) Finset.univ _ (fun i _ =>
      have := isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_moduleCat (J.over Y₀) Λ
        ((Functor.const (Over Y₀)ᵒᵖ).obj M)
      Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (J.over Y₀) _ _)
  obtain ⟨I, V, gg, hVg⟩ := Sieve.exists_eq_ofArrows (Finset.univ.inf
    (fun i : Fin p => Presheaf.imageSieve
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over Y₀) ((Functor.const (Over Y₀)ᵒᵖ).obj M))
      ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i))))
  rw [hVg, GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff, Sieve.overEquiv_ofArrows] at hcov₂
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ hcov₂
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
  rintro Z₂ q ⟨i₀⟩
  have hleft : (gg i₀).left ≫ ww = (V i₀).hom := Over.w (gg i₀)
  have hwit : ∀ i : Fin p, ∃ c : M, (constantUnitApp (J.over Y₀) M (op (V i₀))).hom c =
      (((constantSheaf (J.over Y₀) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj M).obj.map (gg i₀).op).hom
        ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i)) := by
    intro i
    have hmem : (Finset.univ.inf (fun i : Fin p => Presheaf.imageSieve
        (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over Y₀) ((Functor.const (Over Y₀)ᵒᵖ).obj M))
        ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i)))).arrows (gg i₀) := by
      rw [hVg]
      exact Sieve.ofArrows_mk V gg i₀
    exact sieve_apply_of_le (Finset.inf_le (Finset.mem_univ i)) hmem
  choose xx hxx using hwit
  refine isConstantFGOver_X₂_of_lifts hS hM (restrictTrivIso J Λ (V i₀).hom M α)
    (restrictTrivIso J Λ (V i₀).hom N β) y hy (fun i => ((κ' i : Fin m → Λ))) hκ
    (fun j => (S.X₂.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom (t j)) xx ?_ ?_
  · intro j
    have hnat : (S.g.hom.app (op (V i₀).left)).hom
          ((S.X₂.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom (t j)) =
        (S.X₃.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom ((S.g.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom (t j)) :=
      ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (S.g.hom.naturality (gg i₀).left.op) (t j)
    rw [hnat, ht j, trivSection_restrictTrivIso]
    exact trivSectionAt_comp ww (gg i₀).left (y j) |>.trans (by rw [hleft])
  · intro i
    have hα : (α.hom.hom.app (op (V i₀))).hom
          ((constantUnitApp (J.over Y₀) M (op (V i₀))).hom (xx i)) =
        (S.X₁.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom (uu i) := by
      have hnat : (α.hom.hom.app (op (V i₀))).hom
            ((((constantSheaf (J.over Y₀) (ModuleCat.{max u v w} Λ)).obj M).obj.map
              (gg i₀).op).hom ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i))) =
          (S.X₁.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom
            ((α.hom.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom
              ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i))) :=
        ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (α.hom.hom.naturality (gg i₀).op)
          ((α.inv.hom.app (op (Over.mk ww))).hom (uu i))
      rw [hxx i, hnat]
      exact congrArg (S.X₁.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom
        (iso_app_inv_app α (op (Over.mk ww)) _)
    have hfnat : (S.f.hom.app (op (V i₀).left)).hom
          ((S.X₁.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom (uu i)) =
        (S.X₂.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom ((S.f.hom.app (op Z₁)).hom (uu i)) :=
      ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (S.f.hom.naturality (gg i₀).left.op) (uu i)
    rw [trivSection_restrictTrivIso, show (trivSectionAt α (V i₀).hom).hom (xx i) =
        (S.X₁.obj.map (gg i₀).left.op).hom (uu i) from hα, hfnat, huu i, map_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [map_smul]

end Closure

/-! ### The weak Serre subcategory -/

section WeakSerre

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ] [IsNoetherianRing Λ]

/-- **Closure under extensions.** The finite type locally constant sheaves of `Λ`-modules are
closed under extensions: over an object trivializing both ends of a short exact sequence, the
middle term is trivialized on a covering family, and local constancy is a local condition. -/
@[sga "4 IX 2.1" "(iii), modules"]
instance isClosedUnderExtensions_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf :
    ObjectProperty.IsClosedUnderExtensions
      (IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf.{v, u, w} J Λ) where
  prop_X₂_of_shortExact {S} hS h₁ h₃ := by
    rw [isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf_iff_trivSieve_mem] at h₁ h₃ ⊢
    intro U
    exact J.transitive (J.intersection_covering (h₁ U) (h₃ U)) _
      fun _ _ hp => trivSieve_X₂_mem hS hp.1 hp.2

/-- **Stacks Tag 093U (3).** On a site, the finite type locally constant sheaves of modules over
a Noetherian ring form a weak Serre subcategory of the category of sheaves of modules.

The five conditions of Tag 0754 are: strict fullness
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isClosedUnderIsomorphisms_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf`),
containment of `0`
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.containsZero_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf`), closure under
kernels and under cokernels
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isClosedUnderKernels_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf` and
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isClosedUnderCokernels_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf`), and
closure under extensions
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isClosedUnderExtensions_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf`). -/
@[stacks 093U "finite_type_modules", sga "4 IX 2.1" "(ii) ker/coker, (iii)"]
instance isWeakSerreClass_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf :
    ObjectProperty.IsWeakSerreClass
      (IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf.{v, u, w} J Λ) :=
  isWeakSerreClass_of_isClosedUnderExtensions J Λ

end WeakSerre

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf

